<section class="relay-map" aria-labelledby="relay-map-title" data-reveal>
  <div class="shell">
    <header class="relay-map__heading">
      <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--pill">THE ACCESS BOUNDARY</p>
      <h2 id="relay-map-title">One mailbox. <em>Two very different</em> routes.</h2>
      <p>Direct mailbox access gives an agent broad upstream authority. SirenoRELAY accepts a separate bearer token, applies current policy, and returns only permitted results.</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="relay-map__stage" aria-describedby="relay-map-caption">
      <div class="relay-route relay-route--direct">
        <div class="route-label"><span class="route-label__dot"></span><b>Direct mailbox access</b><small>Agent holds upstream credentials</small></div>
        <div class="iso-scene" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="iso-platform iso-platform--risk"></div>
          <div class="iso-object iso-agent iso-agent--risk"><span>AI</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="iso-object iso-mailbox iso-mailbox--risk"><span>MAIL</span><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="iso-flow iso-flow--risk"><i class="packet packet--credentials">credentials</i><i class="packet packet--mail">all folders</i><i class="packet packet--attachment">attachments</i></div>
          <div class="iso-caption iso-caption--agent">AUTONOMOUS<br />AGENT</div>
          <div class="iso-caption iso-caption--mail">UPSTREAM<br />MAILBOX</div>
          <div class="iso-warning">Unrestricted connection</div>
        </div>
        <p class="route-copy">The agent can use the mailbox credential directly. Folder and sender policy is not applied at the relay boundary, and sends bypass relay recipient checks.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="relay-route relay-route--protected">
        <div class="route-label"><span class="route-label__dot"></span><b>Protected relay gateway</b><small>Scoped bearer token + current policy</small></div>
        <div class="iso-scene" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="iso-platform iso-platform--safe"></div>
          <div class="iso-object iso-agent iso-agent--safe"><span>AI</span><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="iso-object iso-gate"><span>Sireno</span><strong>RELAY</strong><i>policy</i></div>
          <div class="iso-object iso-mailbox iso-mailbox--safe"><span>MAIL</span><i></i><i></i></div>
          <div class="iso-flow iso-flow--token"><i class="packet packet--token">bearer token</i></div>
          <div class="iso-flow iso-flow--allowed"><i class="packet packet--allowed">allowed mail</i><i class="packet packet--allowed packet--two">filtered result</i></div>
          <div class="iso-flow iso-flow--blocked"><i class="packet packet--blocked">denied</i></div>
          <div class="iso-caption iso-caption--agent">AGENT</div>
          <div class="iso-caption iso-caption--gate">TOKEN + POLICY<br />CHECKPOINT</div>
          <div class="iso-caption iso-caption--mail">OWNER-CONTROLLED<br />MAILBOX</div>
          <div class="iso-warning iso-warning--safe">Credentials stay with the relay</div>
        </div>
        <p class="route-copy">SirenoRELAY owns upstream credentials, authenticates the agent token, filters folders and messages, and checks outbound recipients before handoff.</p>
      </div>
      <figcaption id="relay-map-caption">The animation is a simplified request path. SirenoRELAY is not a sandbox for an agent that can access the relay host, configuration, or upstream mail server directly.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
